# Netlify: every page address is served by the single-page app. Real files
# (assets, content.js) are always served first; a missing file under /assets
# is a real 404 instead of the page, as on Vercel and with dev.mjs.
# Cloudflare Pages doesn't use these rules (it rejects the last one as a loop):
# there, delete 404.html instead and every page address gets index.html.
/assets/*  /404.html     404
/*         /index.html   200
